    {
     "tipo": "explicacion",
     "titulo": "へ emphasises the direction; に introduces the destination. With many movement verbs they can be used interchangeably.",
     "texto": [
      "With 行きます, 来ます and 帰ります, both へ and に can mark the destination. へ is read e when it works as a particle.",
      "わたし は にほん へ いきます。 (I'm going to Japan.)",
      "ともだち は うち に きます。 (My friend is coming to my house.)"
     ],
